Database and migration plan
The preferred design is additive without a new branch-view session table. The viewer context is ephemeral browser state, and the durable sources of truth already exist: TenantLocation, UserLocationGrant, terminal registry data, PosTerminalShift, operator-session data when enabled, and audit_logs. Avoid persisting a fake viewer shift.Likely no schema migration is needed for the basic branch directory and viewer context if existing tables and audit columns are present.
If a new pos:branch_view permission is added to the permission catalog, update role catalogs and run the repository-approved additive permission backfill/reconciliation. Do not mass-revoke existing grants automatically.
If the branch directory exposes current operator status, verify the operator-session migration is present in every supported tenant schema. Missing schema must return an explicit unavailable state, not an empty "no cashier" result.
Add indexes only when query plans show need, likely on open shift location/status and operator-session location/active state. Confirm existing indexes before adding duplicates.
Any schema change must be implemented in apps/dgfy-migration-runner and reflected in tenant schema synchronization where required. The plan does not authorize a migration yet.
